-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The model files are not covered by the license above.

A .pkf file that tools/pkito-tools writes holds the weights of one of NVIDIA's
Parakeet TDT checkpoints, rounded to int8 and rearranged, and those weights
are NVIDIA's, under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):

  parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
  parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3

Whoever shares a .pkf shares those weights, modified, and owes NVIDIA the
attribution CC-BY-4.0 asks for; every .pkf carries it in its "notice"
metadata (`pkito info` prints it). The architecture core/ implements is
NeMo's (https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/NeMo, Apache-2.0), reimplemented from
its description and its code's arithmetic, without NeMo's code.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A .pkf also holds Silero VAD's weights, and core/vad.c and core/segment.c
are a port of Silero VAD's model and of its two state machines (by way of
vadito, whose code core/wav.c, core/resample.c and core/vmath.h also come
from, under the MIT license above). Silero's notice:

